1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,449
Sweetheart, I have a confession.

2
00:00:02,629 --> 00:00:04,052
For twenty years,

3
00:00:04,052 --> 00:00:07,066
my gingerbread men were hard as roof

4
00:00:07,066 --> 00:00:07,819
shingles.

5
00:00:07,999 --> 00:00:10,886
My grandchildren used them as hockey pucks

6
00:00:10,886 --> 00:00:12,329
on the kitchen floor.

7
00:00:12,509 --> 00:00:15,574
My son-in-law said he chipped a tooth.

8
00:00:15,754 --> 00:00:17,121
And all that time,

9
00:00:17,121 --> 00:00:20,384
the recipe for soft gingerbread was sitting

10
00:00:20,384 --> 00:00:23,344
in Grandma Pearl's handwriting in a tin

11
00:00:23,344 --> 00:00:24,938
box in my own pantry.

12
00:00:25,118 --> 00:00:26,848
I just never looked.

13
00:00:27,198 --> 00:00:30,663
So tonight I'm giving you Pearl's gingerbread

14
00:00:30,663 --> 00:00:30,971
men.

15
00:00:31,151 --> 00:00:33,248
Soft and chewy in the middle,

16
00:00:33,248 --> 00:00:35,273
a little crisp on the edges,

17
00:00:35,273 --> 00:00:38,310
with that deep molasses flavor that smells

18
00:00:38,310 --> 00:00:41,131
like Christmas the minute the oven door

19
00:00:41,131 --> 00:00:41,565
opens.

20
00:00:41,745 --> 00:00:44,005
Every ingredient, every step,

21
00:00:44,005 --> 00:00:47,356
and the mistakes that turn gingerbread into

22
00:00:47,356 --> 00:00:47,979
a brick.

23
00:00:48,159 --> 00:00:49,781
Get your pencil,

24
00:00:49,781 --> 00:00:50,389
honey.

25
00:00:50,569 --> 00:00:51,877
And stay with me,

26
00:00:51,877 --> 00:00:55,495
because Pearl's third secret surprised me most,

27
00:00:55,495 --> 00:00:57,651
and it's the easiest of all.

28
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:01,063
Grandma Pearl kept her recipes on index

29
00:01:01,063 --> 00:01:03,341
cards in a green tin box with

30
00:01:03,341 --> 00:01:04,990
a rooster on the lid.

31
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:08,224
The gingerbread card is stained brown with

32
00:01:08,224 --> 00:01:10,843
molasses, and on the back she wrote,

33
00:01:10,843 --> 00:01:13,970
nineteen thirty-eight, for the church sale.

34
00:01:14,150 --> 00:01:15,799
During the Depression,

35
00:01:15,799 --> 00:01:18,198
molasses was cheaper than sugar,

36
00:01:18,198 --> 00:01:21,347
so gingerbread was the Christmas cookie of

37
00:01:21,347 --> 00:01:22,022
the poor.

38
00:01:22,202 --> 00:01:24,355
And she said it was the best

39
00:01:24,355 --> 00:01:24,663
one.

40
00:01:25,013 --> 00:01:26,137
In our house,

41
00:01:26,137 --> 00:01:29,424
the gingerbread men were for the tree.

42
00:01:29,604 --> 00:01:31,866
My mother tied a red ribbon around

43
00:01:31,866 --> 00:01:33,995
each one's neck and hung them on

44
00:01:33,995 --> 00:01:35,259
the lower branches,

45
00:01:35,259 --> 00:01:37,255
where Danny and I could reach.

46
00:01:37,435 --> 00:01:38,369
The rule was,

47
00:01:38,369 --> 00:01:40,093
you could eat one a day,

48
00:01:40,093 --> 00:01:42,033
from the first of December.

49
00:01:42,213 --> 00:01:44,983
By Christmas there were only three left,

50
00:01:44,983 --> 00:01:46,369
all on the very top,

51
00:01:46,369 --> 00:01:48,654
where my father had moved them to

52
00:01:48,654 --> 00:01:50,317
protect them from Danny.

53
00:01:50,667 --> 00:01:52,366
The year Danny was nine,

54
00:01:52,366 --> 00:01:54,914
he ate the gingerbread man meant for

55
00:01:54,914 --> 00:01:56,684
the very top of the tree,

56
00:01:56,684 --> 00:01:58,879
the big one with the gold sugar

57
00:01:58,879 --> 00:02:01,428
buttons, and he hid the ribbon under

58
00:02:01,428 --> 00:02:02,207
his pillow.

59
00:02:02,387 --> 00:02:04,783
My mother found it on Christmas Eve

60
00:02:04,783 --> 00:02:07,042
when she was changing the sheets.

61
00:02:07,222 --> 00:02:08,813
She didn't say a word.

62
00:02:08,993 --> 00:02:10,380
On Christmas morning,

63
00:02:10,380 --> 00:02:13,089
Danny's stocking had a gingerbread man in

64
00:02:13,089 --> 00:02:15,402
it, with a note in her handwriting.

65
00:02:15,582 --> 00:02:16,847
You owe me one.

66
00:02:17,027 --> 00:02:19,585
He laughed about that note for fifty

67
00:02:19,585 --> 00:02:20,011
years.

68
00:02:20,361 --> 00:02:22,076
Here's what you need,

69
00:02:22,076 --> 00:02:22,566
honey.

70
00:02:22,746 --> 00:02:24,453
Three cups of flour.

71
00:02:24,633 --> 00:02:27,487
One and a half teaspoons of baking

72
00:02:27,487 --> 00:02:27,907
soda.

73
00:02:28,087 --> 00:02:31,041
One tablespoon of ground ginger,

74
00:02:31,041 --> 00:02:33,625
and yes, a whole tablespoon.

75
00:02:33,805 --> 00:02:36,708
One and a half teaspoons of cinnamon.

76
00:02:36,888 --> 00:02:39,755
A quarter teaspoon of ground cloves.

77
00:02:39,935 --> 00:02:42,164
And half a teaspoon of salt.

78
00:02:42,344 --> 00:02:44,817
Stir all that together in one bowl.

79
00:02:45,168 --> 00:02:46,398
In another bowl.

80
00:02:46,578 --> 00:02:49,075
Three quarters of a cup of butter,

81
00:02:49,075 --> 00:02:49,736
softened.

82
00:02:49,916 --> 00:02:52,421
Three quarters of a cup of dark

83
00:02:52,421 --> 00:02:54,038
brown sugar, packed.

84
00:02:54,218 --> 00:02:55,297
One egg.

85
00:02:55,477 --> 00:02:57,536
Half a cup of molasses,

86
00:02:57,536 --> 00:02:59,057
the regular kind,

87
00:02:59,057 --> 00:03:00,400
not blackstrap.

88
00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:02,143
Blackstrap is bitter,

89
00:03:02,143 --> 00:03:05,344
honey, and it's the reason some gingerbread

90
00:03:05,344 --> 00:03:06,907
tastes like medicine.

91
00:03:07,087 --> 00:03:09,456
And one teaspoon of vanilla.

92
00:03:09,806 --> 00:03:13,184
Notice, sweetheart, the brown sugar.

93
00:03:13,364 --> 00:03:17,172
Most gingerbread recipes use white sugar.

94
00:03:17,352 --> 00:03:19,542
Brown sugar holds moisture,

95
00:03:19,542 --> 00:03:22,544
and that's Pearl's first secret for a

96
00:03:22,544 --> 00:03:23,517
soft cookie.

97
00:03:23,697 --> 00:03:25,961
The molasses does the same.

98
00:03:26,141 --> 00:03:28,631
Together they keep the middle chewy for

99
00:03:28,631 --> 00:03:29,461
a whole week.

100
00:03:29,641 --> 00:03:32,021
In a minute I'll tell you Pearl's

101
00:03:32,021 --> 00:03:34,690
second secret, the one that made mine

102
00:03:34,690 --> 00:03:37,141
hard as shingles for twenty years.

103
00:03:37,492 --> 00:03:39,677
And use fresh spices,

104
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:40,301
honey.

105
00:03:40,481 --> 00:03:42,563
That jar of ginger in the back

106
00:03:42,563 --> 00:03:45,547
of your cupboard from three Christmases ago

107
00:03:45,547 --> 00:03:46,727
tastes like dust.

108
00:03:46,907 --> 00:03:50,142
Ground spices lose their flavor after about

109
00:03:50,142 --> 00:03:50,669
a year.

110
00:03:50,849 --> 00:03:51,534
Smell it.

111
00:03:51,714 --> 00:03:54,606
If it doesn't make your nose tingle,

112
00:03:54,606 --> 00:03:55,731
buy a new jar.

113
00:03:55,911 --> 00:03:58,987
It's the difference between gingerbread that tastes

114
00:03:58,987 --> 00:04:01,821
like Christmas and gingerbread that tastes like

115
00:04:01,821 --> 00:04:02,424
cardboard.

116
00:04:02,775 --> 00:04:05,480
And measure the molasses this way.

117
00:04:05,660 --> 00:04:08,060
Rub the inside of your measuring cup

118
00:04:08,060 --> 00:04:10,327
with a little butter or oil first.

119
00:04:10,507 --> 00:04:12,790
The molasses slides right out,

120
00:04:12,790 --> 00:04:15,682
every drop, instead of sticking to the

121
00:04:15,682 --> 00:04:15,987
cup.

122
00:04:16,167 --> 00:04:18,284
Pearl did it with a scrap of

123
00:04:18,284 --> 00:04:19,267
butter paper.

124
00:04:19,447 --> 00:04:22,494
You'd be surprised how much molasses people

125
00:04:22,494 --> 00:04:23,699
leave in the cup,

126
00:04:23,699 --> 00:04:26,534
and then wonder why their gingerbread is

127
00:04:26,534 --> 00:04:26,889
pale.

128
00:04:27,239 --> 00:04:28,318
Step one.

129
00:04:28,498 --> 00:04:31,234
Beat the butter and brown sugar until

130
00:04:31,234 --> 00:04:33,378
smooth, then beat in the egg,

131
00:04:33,378 --> 00:04:35,522
the molasses and the vanilla.

132
00:04:35,702 --> 00:04:37,455
It will look a little curdled.

133
00:04:37,635 --> 00:04:39,493
Don't worry about that.

134
00:04:39,673 --> 00:04:42,477
Then add the flour mixture in three

135
00:04:42,477 --> 00:04:45,602
parts, mixing slowly until it's all one

136
00:04:45,602 --> 00:04:46,964
soft, dark dough.

137
00:04:47,144 --> 00:04:48,769
It will be sticky.

138
00:04:48,949 --> 00:04:49,994
That's right.

139
00:04:50,174 --> 00:04:51,720
If this is helping you,

140
00:04:51,720 --> 00:04:54,006
honey, tap the like button for me.

141
00:04:54,186 --> 00:04:56,844
It helps Grandma more than you know.

142
00:04:57,195 --> 00:04:58,332
Step two.

143
00:04:58,512 --> 00:05:00,008
Divide it in half,

144
00:05:00,008 --> 00:05:02,585
pat each half into a flat disk,

145
00:05:02,585 --> 00:05:04,912
wrap it in wax paper and put

146
00:05:04,912 --> 00:05:07,323
it in the icebox for at least

147
00:05:07,323 --> 00:05:09,484
three hours, or overnight.

148
00:05:09,664 --> 00:05:12,449
Gingerbread dough is soft and sticky,

149
00:05:12,449 --> 00:05:14,482
and you can't roll it warm.

150
00:05:14,662 --> 00:05:17,135
Cold, it rolls like a dream.

151
00:05:17,485 --> 00:05:18,611
Step three.

152
00:05:18,791 --> 00:05:21,461
Heat the oven to three hundred fifty.

153
00:05:21,641 --> 00:05:24,017
Roll the dough between two sheets of

154
00:05:24,017 --> 00:05:26,262
parchment to a quarter inch thick.

155
00:05:26,442 --> 00:05:29,031
And here's Pearl's second secret.

156
00:05:29,211 --> 00:05:30,346
A quarter inch,

157
00:05:30,346 --> 00:05:31,254
not thinner.

158
00:05:31,434 --> 00:05:34,292
Thin gingerbread bakes hard and crisp,

159
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:37,226
and that's what made mine like shingles

160
00:05:37,226 --> 00:05:38,505
for twenty years.

161
00:05:38,685 --> 00:05:40,934
I was rolling it thin as a

162
00:05:40,934 --> 00:05:41,367
dime.

163
00:05:41,717 --> 00:05:42,843
Step four.

164
00:05:43,023 --> 00:05:44,013
Cut your men,

165
00:05:44,013 --> 00:05:47,212
lift them onto a parchment-lined sheet two

166
00:05:47,212 --> 00:05:50,030
inches apart, and press in raisins or

167
00:05:50,030 --> 00:05:53,000
little candies for the eyes and buttons

168
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:54,447
now, before baking.

169
00:05:54,627 --> 00:05:56,235
If you want to hang them,

170
00:05:56,235 --> 00:05:57,844
poke a hole at the top of

171
00:05:57,844 --> 00:05:59,259
the head with a straw.

172
00:05:59,610 --> 00:06:02,605
Step five, Pearl's third secret.

173
00:06:02,785 --> 00:06:05,383
Bake them for only eight minutes,

174
00:06:05,383 --> 00:06:06,721
nine at the most.

175
00:06:06,901 --> 00:06:09,834
They'll look soft and puffy and not

176
00:06:09,834 --> 00:06:10,755
quite done.

177
00:06:10,935 --> 00:06:12,816
Take them out anyway.

178
00:06:12,996 --> 00:06:15,496
They keep cooking on the hot pan,

179
00:06:15,496 --> 00:06:17,768
and they firm up as they cool.

180
00:06:17,948 --> 00:06:19,782
If they look done in the oven,

181
00:06:19,782 --> 00:06:21,617
they're overdone on the plate.

182
00:06:21,967 --> 00:06:23,830
Let them sit on the pan for

183
00:06:23,830 --> 00:06:26,177
five minutes before you move them,

184
00:06:26,177 --> 00:06:28,317
or the arms and legs break off.

185
00:06:28,497 --> 00:06:30,262
Then cool them on a rack.

186
00:06:30,442 --> 00:06:32,465
And put the broken ones on a

187
00:06:32,465 --> 00:06:33,983
plate for the bakers.

188
00:06:34,163 --> 00:06:36,299
That's the law in my kitchen.

189
00:06:36,479 --> 00:06:38,686
But first, let me show you how

190
00:06:38,686 --> 00:06:40,599
to tell when they're done,

191
00:06:40,599 --> 00:06:43,689
because that's where most people go wrong.

192
00:06:44,039 --> 00:06:46,242
Here's how to know they're done,

193
00:06:46,242 --> 00:06:46,999
sweetheart.

194
00:06:47,179 --> 00:06:49,684
Press the middle of one very gently

195
00:06:49,684 --> 00:06:51,115
with your fingertip.

196
00:06:51,295 --> 00:06:53,652
If it leaves a little dent that

197
00:06:53,652 --> 00:06:55,173
stays, it's perfect.

198
00:06:55,353 --> 00:06:58,034
If it springs right back and feels

199
00:06:58,034 --> 00:07:01,030
firm, it's already a little overbaked.

200
00:07:01,210 --> 00:07:03,799
Next sheet, take a minute off.

201
00:07:03,979 --> 00:07:05,895
Every oven is different.

202
00:07:06,075 --> 00:07:08,112
Mine runs hot on the left,

203
00:07:08,112 --> 00:07:10,777
so I turn the pan halfway through.

204
00:07:11,127 --> 00:07:12,482
So the mistakes,

205
00:07:12,482 --> 00:07:13,414
sweetheart.

206
00:07:13,594 --> 00:07:16,125
Mistake one, rolling them too thin.

207
00:07:16,305 --> 00:07:19,509
Mistake two, baking until they look done.

208
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:23,439
Mistake three, white sugar instead of brown.

209
00:07:23,619 --> 00:07:25,005
And mistake four,

210
00:07:25,005 --> 00:07:27,450
too much flour on the counter.

211
00:07:27,630 --> 00:07:30,035
Every handful of flour you roll into

212
00:07:30,035 --> 00:07:31,705
the dough makes it drier.

213
00:07:31,885 --> 00:07:34,776
That's why I roll between parchment.

214
00:07:34,956 --> 00:07:36,988
No extra flour at all.

215
00:07:37,338 --> 00:07:38,533
And one more.

216
00:07:38,713 --> 00:07:40,977
Storing them with crisp cookies.

217
00:07:41,157 --> 00:07:44,219
Soft gingerbread and crisp sugar cookies in

218
00:07:44,219 --> 00:07:45,144
the same tin,

219
00:07:45,144 --> 00:07:47,636
and in two days they're both wrong.

220
00:07:47,816 --> 00:07:50,137
Keep gingerbread in its own tin,

221
00:07:50,137 --> 00:07:52,095
and put a slice of bread or

222
00:07:52,095 --> 00:07:54,271
a piece of apple in with them.

223
00:07:54,451 --> 00:07:56,961
The cookies pull the moisture from it

224
00:07:56,961 --> 00:07:57,911
and stay soft.

225
00:07:58,091 --> 00:08:00,169
Change it every few days.

226
00:08:00,519 --> 00:08:02,346
If they do come out hard,

227
00:08:02,346 --> 00:08:04,466
honey, don't throw them away.

228
00:08:04,646 --> 00:08:06,416
Put them in a tin with a

229
00:08:06,416 --> 00:08:08,261
slice of bread overnight,

230
00:08:08,261 --> 00:08:10,695
and most of them soften right up.

231
00:08:10,875 --> 00:08:12,606
And the ones that don't,

232
00:08:12,606 --> 00:08:15,203
crush them up and sprinkle them over

233
00:08:15,203 --> 00:08:16,502
vanilla ice cream,

234
00:08:16,502 --> 00:08:19,243
or use them instead of graham crackers

235
00:08:19,243 --> 00:08:20,325
in a pie crust.

236
00:08:20,505 --> 00:08:23,622
Pearl's gingerbread crust for pumpkin pie came

237
00:08:23,622 --> 00:08:25,993
from a batch she burned in nineteen

238
00:08:25,993 --> 00:08:26,670
fifty-two.

239
00:08:27,021 --> 00:08:28,105
For the icing,

240
00:08:28,105 --> 00:08:30,738
one cup of powdered sugar with one

241
00:08:30,738 --> 00:08:33,371
tablespoon of milk and a few drops

242
00:08:33,371 --> 00:08:34,532
of lemon juice.

243
00:08:34,712 --> 00:08:36,401
It should be thick,

244
00:08:36,401 --> 00:08:37,824
like toothpaste.

245
00:08:38,004 --> 00:08:39,968
Put it in a sandwich bag,

246
00:08:39,968 --> 00:08:41,853
snip the tiniest corner,

247
00:08:41,853 --> 00:08:43,345
and pipe the faces,

248
00:08:43,345 --> 00:08:46,331
the buttons, and the little zigzags on

249
00:08:46,331 --> 00:08:47,744
the arms and legs.

250
00:08:47,924 --> 00:08:50,089
Let them dry for a few hours

251
00:08:50,089 --> 00:08:51,326
before stacking.

252
00:08:51,506 --> 00:08:52,807
And in a minute,

253
00:08:52,807 --> 00:08:53,944
the best part.

254
00:08:54,124 --> 00:08:55,100
The children.

255
00:08:55,450 --> 00:08:57,149
Let the children do it,

256
00:08:57,149 --> 00:08:59,513
honey, and don't fix their work.

257
00:08:59,693 --> 00:09:02,397
A gingerbread man with three eyes and

258
00:09:02,397 --> 00:09:04,881
a crooked smile is worth more than

259
00:09:04,881 --> 00:09:05,904
a perfect one.

260
00:09:06,084 --> 00:09:09,452
My granddaughter made one in nineteen ninety-four

261
00:09:09,452 --> 00:09:11,720
with a mustache and a cowboy hat,

262
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:13,988
and we still talk about him every

263
00:09:13,988 --> 00:09:14,676
Christmas.

264
00:09:14,856 --> 00:09:16,876
We called him Uncle Earl.

265
00:09:17,226 --> 00:09:19,250
And if you want the house to

266
00:09:19,250 --> 00:09:20,768
smell like Christmas,

267
00:09:20,768 --> 00:09:23,877
sweetheart, bake one batch in the afternoon

268
00:09:23,877 --> 00:09:25,829
right before company comes.

269
00:09:26,009 --> 00:09:28,301
Nothing in a candle or a spray

270
00:09:28,301 --> 00:09:31,129
smells like warm ginger and molasses.

271
00:09:31,309 --> 00:09:32,799
When people walk in,

272
00:09:32,799 --> 00:09:35,034
they stop in the hall and say,

273
00:09:35,034 --> 00:09:36,301
oh, what is that?

274
00:09:36,481 --> 00:09:38,129
That's the moment you want.

275
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:40,446
The dough keeps a week in the

276
00:09:40,446 --> 00:09:43,091
icebox, or three months in the freezer,

277
00:09:43,091 --> 00:09:44,041
wrapped tight.

278
00:09:44,221 --> 00:09:46,824
Baked cookies stay soft for about a

279
00:09:46,824 --> 00:09:48,906
week in a tin with the apple

280
00:09:48,906 --> 00:09:49,352
slice.

281
00:09:49,532 --> 00:09:51,464
And they mail beautifully,

282
00:09:51,464 --> 00:09:53,916
packed in a tin with crumpled wax

283
00:09:53,916 --> 00:09:56,814
paper, because they don't break the way

284
00:09:56,814 --> 00:09:58,077
crisp cookies do.

285
00:09:58,257 --> 00:10:01,297
My mother mailed gingerbread to my father's

286
00:10:01,297 --> 00:10:04,054
army friends every year until they were

287
00:10:04,054 --> 00:10:04,620
old men.

288
00:10:04,970 --> 00:10:07,600
And a gingerbread tip for the little

289
00:10:07,600 --> 00:10:07,965
ones.

290
00:10:08,145 --> 00:10:10,818
Give each child a plain gingerbread man

291
00:10:10,818 --> 00:10:13,216
with their name piped on his belly,

292
00:10:13,216 --> 00:10:15,203
and hide one at each place at

293
00:10:15,203 --> 00:10:16,574
the Christmas table.

294
00:10:16,754 --> 00:10:19,138
Or tie one to each present under

295
00:10:19,138 --> 00:10:20,852
the tree as a name tag.

296
00:10:21,032 --> 00:10:23,813
My grandchildren look for their gingerbread man

297
00:10:23,813 --> 00:10:25,943
before they look for their presents.

298
00:10:26,123 --> 00:10:28,654
They know which is theirs before they

299
00:10:28,654 --> 00:10:29,269
can read.

300
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:31,164
So one more time,

301
00:10:31,164 --> 00:10:31,709
honey.

302
00:10:31,889 --> 00:10:34,850
Brown sugar and regular molasses.

303
00:10:35,030 --> 00:10:37,259
A whole tablespoon of ginger.

304
00:10:37,439 --> 00:10:38,658
Chill the dough.

305
00:10:38,838 --> 00:10:41,210
Roll it a quarter inch thick between

306
00:10:41,210 --> 00:10:41,868
parchment.

307
00:10:42,048 --> 00:10:44,606
Eight minutes, and take them out while

308
00:10:44,606 --> 00:10:46,019
they still look soft.

309
00:10:46,199 --> 00:10:48,428
Store them alone with a slice of

310
00:10:48,428 --> 00:10:48,846
apple.

311
00:10:49,026 --> 00:10:50,948
That's Pearl's gingerbread,

312
00:10:50,948 --> 00:10:53,083
and nobody will ever use it as

313
00:10:53,083 --> 00:10:54,506
a hockey puck again.

314
00:10:54,856 --> 00:10:56,989
Tell me in the comments,

315
00:10:56,989 --> 00:10:57,967
sweetheart.

316
00:10:58,147 --> 00:11:00,206
Do you bite the head off first,

317
00:11:00,206 --> 00:11:01,003
or the feet?

318
00:11:01,183 --> 00:11:04,087
My father always started with the feet,

319
00:11:04,087 --> 00:11:07,139
so the gingerbread man couldn't run away.

320
00:11:07,319 --> 00:11:09,200
I read every comment.

321
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:11,870
And if you want another one tonight,

322
00:11:11,870 --> 00:11:14,774
the whole playlist of Grandma's recipes is

323
00:11:14,774 --> 00:11:16,642
right there on your screen,

324
00:11:16,642 --> 00:11:18,578
and I'll see you in the next

325
00:11:18,578 --> 00:11:18,993
video.

326
00:11:19,173 --> 00:11:20,752
Good night, honey.

327
00:11:20,932 --> 00:11:22,430
Merry Christmas.
